{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3059","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3059","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3059\",\"parent_revision\":\"116e1120c77ce4d95f406af30c6802793df09cc610d46735ecef089e4d2f013f\",\"root_revision\":\"116e1120c77ce4d95f406af30c6802793df09cc610d46735ecef089e4d2f013f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe address-based navigation path imports the engine's parser and indexer, then reimplements navigation and pagination on top of them. The engine's own navigation and pagination layer has no consumers.\\n\\nOne consequence is already visible: the map drops deep addresses when over budget and documents them as still resolvable, which R2 forbids \u2014 nothing may be dropped or elided to fit a budget.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Navigation and pagination are served by the engine, not reimplemented\\n- [ ] The map paginates rather than dropping addresses; every address is reachable on some page\\n- [ ] Reimplemented navigation code is deleted\\n- [ ] Existing address grammar and response shapes continue to work for current callers\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verified Evidence The Map Is Unbounded Not Merely Lossy\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe map handler in `disclosure_handler.py` assembles its output as:\\n\\n```python\\nmap_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(mapper.format_map_line(e) for e in entries)\\n```\\n\\nEvery entry, joined. No budget check, no truncation, no pagination. An `over_budget` boolean is computed alongside and the full text is returned regardless.\\n\\nThree separate places assert a bound that does not exist:\\n\\n- the map response type's own docstring states the text is always under roughly 2,000 tokens regardless of item size\\n- `docs/mcp-progressive-disclosure-contract.md` described the text as bounded by the token budget, with deep addresses absent but still resolvable\\n- the agent-facing documentation added in PR #3051 repeated the bound as a guarantee (being corrected on that PR)\\n\\nSo the earlier characterisation of this as an invented-limit problem was wrong in the safer direction: nothing is dropped because nothing is bounded. A map for a large item exceeds a harness response cap outright rather than degrading.\\n\\nAdds to this item's acceptance criteria: the map response is bounded and paginated, and no docstring or document asserts a bound the implementation does not enforce.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"941d2cd39c2b6baa3c81320d462ea3c0552fc466ac84c4048d2515d50c43c93a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvbxTw\"}"}